{#
| Variable                | Type          | Description                 |
|-------------------------|---------------|-----------------------------|
| page                    | object        |                             |
| page.title              | string        |                             |
| page.slug               | string        |                             |
| slides                  | ?Article[]    | @see pages/blog/single.twig |
| articles                | Article[]     |                             |
| categories              | BlogCategory[]|                             |
| category.is_current     | bool          |                             |
| category.name           | string        |                             |
| category.url            | string        |                             |

UNIX (ROADMAP 5.4 · DS §8.41 · D100): unix.sa main-blog (templates/blog.json). One visible h1 (the page title)
on every blog page, categories as a row of real links (no sidebar / dropdown JS), Salla's featured `slides` as
up to two large cards instead of Raed's slider, then the archive in a 1 / 2 / 3-column grid. Paging stays with
Salla's salla-infinite-scroll (its «load more» button is an <a href> to the next page; no autoload, so the URL
doesn't change while reading). Cards: components/blog/unix-article-card.twig.
#}
{% extends "layouts.master" %}

{% block content %}
  {% set unix_featured = slides|default([])|slice(0, 2) %}
  {# «كل المقالات» is current only on the main blog index: not on a category, and (via is_page) not on tag or
     author archives. If Salla reports those as blog.index too, the chip is still marked there (D100). #}
  {% set unix_has_current = not is_page('blog.index') %}
  {% for category in categories|default([]) %}
    {% if category.is_current %}{% set unix_has_current = true %}{% endif %}
  {% endfor %}

  <div class="unix-container unix-blog-index">
    {# add breadcumbs container in pages to make a space in case breadcrumbs is off #}
    <nav class="breadcrumbs w-full py-5">
      <salla-breadcrumb></salla-breadcrumb>
    </nav>

    <header class="unix-blog-index__head">
      {# ROADMAP 3.11 · DS §14.2: the page's single h1, always visible #}
      <h1 class="unix-blog-index__title">{{ page.title }}</h1>

      {% if categories|default([])|length %}
        <nav class="unix-blog-index__cats" aria-label="{{ trans('blocks.unix.blog.categories') }}">
          <ul class="unix-blog-chips" role="list">
            <li>
              <a class="unix-blog-chip" href="{{ link('blog') }}"{% if not unix_has_current %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ trans('blocks.unix.blog.all') }}</a>
            </li>
            {% for category in categories %}
              <li>
                <a class="unix-blog-chip" href="{{ category.url }}"{% if category.is_current %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ category.name }}</a>
              </li>
            {% endfor %}
          </ul>
        </nav>
      {% endif %}
    </header>

    {% if unix_featured|length %}
      <div class="unix-blog-index__featured">
        {% for article in unix_featured %}
          {% include 'components.blog.unix-article-card' with { article: article, heading: 'h2', featured: true, eager: loop.first } only %}
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    {% endif %}

    {% if articles|length %}
      {% hook 'blog:index.items.start' %}

      <salla-infinite-scroll class="unix-blog-index__grid" next-page="{{ articles.next_page }}">
        {% for article in articles %}
          {% include 'components.blog.unix-article-card' with { article: article, heading: 'h2', eager: loop.first and not unix_featured|length } only %}
        {% endfor %}
      </salla-infinite-scroll>

      {% hook 'blog:index.items.end' %}
    {% elseif not unix_featured|length %}
      {# DS §8.47 shared empty state #}
      <div class="unix-empty">
        <h2 class="unix-empty__title">{{ trans('blocks.unix.blog.empty') }}</h2>
        <a class="unix-btn" href="{{ link('products') }}">{{ trans('blocks.unix.blog.shop') }}</a>
      </div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
{% endblock %}
